# One ProfileInfo whose card-chosen text carries every character a JSON
# string cannot hold raw. profileNickname, serviceProviderName and
# profileName are UTF8String in rsp-2.5.asn: the card picks their
# content, this project does not, and euicc-tools' `card profiles --json`
# embeds all three in its output. So this recording exists to make the
# escaping in that command's json_string provable rather than merely
# plausible -- without it, every fixture in this directory happens to
# hold nothing but plain ASCII letters and spaces, and a json_string that
# escaped nothing at all would pass the whole suite.
#
# The one STORE DATA response is synthetic, produced by the generated
# der_encode (see this directory's README.md for the throwaway program);
# the SELECT ISD-R exchange above it is this card's own real FCI, the
# same bytes every other recording here uses.
#
#   profileNickname       He said "hi" \n is not a newline<TAB><0x01>
#                         -- a quote, a backslash, a tab and a C0
#                            control with no short JSON escape of its
#                            own. The literal backslash-n is there to
#                            catch an escaper that emits it as a real
#                            newline, or one that leaves it alone when
#                            the tab beside it needs escaping.
#   serviceProviderName   Acme<LF>Telco -- an actual newline
#   profileName           Grüße 日本 -- multi-byte UTF-8, which needs no
#                         escaping at all and must come back unmangled;
#                         an escaper that runs per byte would corrupt it.
